  "body": "## What changed\n\n`SdfField::subtract_batch` refuses a chord whose swept window adds more than `MAX_CELLS_PER_MOVE` cells beyond the tool at rest. No caller segmented, so through `Stock` the field engine refused ordinary moves that the column engine cuts.\n\n- `SdfField::subtract_batch_fitted` (new, `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_cut.rs`) is `subtract_batch` with each chord or arc piece whose travel exceeds the ceiling cut as the fewest equal pieces that each fall under it. It finds the count by doubling until the pieces fall under it, then by bisection below that count. A chord splits at equal fractions of its ends. An arc piece splits into equal angular parts on the same circle, with Z shared out evenly (`ArcPiece::split`, `field_arc.rs`). Pieces shorter than one cell shrink no window further, so past that count it refuses by name. A sweep that is neither a chord nor an arc piece cannot be split and refuses by name.\n- The six field arms of `Stock` cut through it, one call each: `simulate_field_with` (`backend.rs`), `simulate_undercut` (`field_undercut.rs`), the lathe arm (`field_lathe.rs`), the display arm (`display.rs`), and the single-move `subtract_flat` and `cut_chord` (`backend_edit.rs`).\n- `subtract_batch` and `subtract` keep the refusal as the bound of one update. The pin `a_wide_tools_long_chord_still_refuses_and_its_segments_cut` now checks that refusal on `subtract_batch` directly, and checks that `subtract_batch_fitted` cuts the same chord. Its block is now `SdfField::from_box` and it cuts the chord once (5.9 s in debug, from 259 s with three mesh-built fields and two cuts).\n\nWhere this differs from the issue: the issue proposed splitting `Move`s in each caller. This PR splits inside the field, at the chord and arc piece, because those are the units the ceiling measures. A move carries an arc, a pose and a C angle, and each caller would need its own interpolation of them. One split there covers every arm. The reasons are in `docs/decisions/4179-segment-to-ceiling.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nSynthetic blocks only, cell 0.254 mm, all in `crates/sim/tests/field_wide_tool.rs`. For the old code, `subtract_batch_fitted` was made to refuse as `subtract_batch` does, which is main's behaviour through `Stock`:\n\n| Test | Old behaviour | This branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| `an_endmills_300_mm_pass_cuts_on_both_engines` (the issue's steps) | fails: the field engine refuses | passes |\n| `a_127_mm_tools_6_mm_plunge_cuts_on_both_engines` | fails: refused | passes |\n| `an_undercut_discs_6_mm_plunge_cuts_through_simulate_undercut` | fails: refused | passes |\n| `a_wide_tools_long_chord_still_refuses_and_its_segments_cut` | fails at the fitted chord | passes |\n| `the_single_move_stock_arms_cut_the_long_chord` (`subtract_flat`, `cut_chord`) | fails: `subtract_flat` refuses (\"segment it\") | passes |\n| `a_127_mm_tools_helical_entry_cuts_on_both_engines` (arc split) | fails: refused (release) | passes (release, 328 s) |\n| `a_wide_tools_short_move_cuts_on_the_field_engine_as_on_the_column_engine` (unchanged) | passes | passes |\n\nThe helical test is in the heavy lane (`#[ignore]`): it takes about 22 min in debug, past the 60 s rule in `AGENTS.md`. It was run by hand with `cargo test --release -p camcraft-sim --test field_wide_tool -- --ignored a_127_mm_tools_helical_entry_cuts_on_both_engines`.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn head `6954260e9` (gates run against upstream/main `903e420b3`):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 85 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (12.7 min).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main`: green, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (26.2 min).\n- No heavy step: this is not a `P1`. No post or toolpath changed, so no example catalog suite.\n\nTrial merge with upstream/main `903e420b3`: clean (`git merge-tree`).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes, apart from the helical test above, run by hand.\n- A tilted tool past the ceiling. It rides the chord path, the same split as the straight pass, but no pin uses a tilt.\n- The lathe arm past the ceiling: it calls the same method, but no pin turns past it.\n- In our own lane (outside this repository), three programs with a 127.4 mm slitting disc plunging 15 to 28 mm were refused before this change. Those programs are not attached; the pins above are the evidence here.\n\nEffort: high (the field simulator's cut of every move).\nChangelog: Stock simulation: the field engine now cuts long passes and deep plunges of wide tools in pieces, instead of refusing moves the column engine cuts.\n\nBranch: from upstream/main `e6849c5ae`; the diff is 9 files in three commits.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4179\n",
